{# Reusable background texture, derived from the Admizz mark's own triangular facets —
   used only on the two navy bookend sections (hero + close). A signature motif, not decoration
   sprinkled everywhere. Pure inline SVG: no raster asset, no JS, scales to any viewport.

   Overscanned 8% top/bottom (vs. a plain inset-0) so main.js can apply a slow ambient
   parallax drift (texture only, never content) without exposing blank edges.

   `w-full` is load-bearing, not decorative: an <svg> is a replaced element, so `inset-x-0`
   (left:0;right:0) alone does NOT stretch its width the way it would a <div> — with no
   intrinsic width/viewBox to size from, it was silently rendering at the UA default replaced-
   element width of exactly 300px and leaving the rest of the section as flat navy. Confirmed
   via getBoundingClientRect(), not eyeballed — see docs/RESUME-PROMPT.md. #}
<svg class="facet-field absolute inset-x-0 w-full pointer-events-none" style="top:-8%; height:116%;" preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid slice" aria-hidden="true">
  <defs>
    <pattern id="admizz-facets" width="72" height="62" patternUnits="userSpaceOnUse">
      <polygon points="36,0 72,20 36,40 0,20" fill="none" stroke="#7C93FF" stroke-width="0.75" opacity="0.20"/>
      <polygon points="36,40 72,60 36,80 0,60" fill="none" stroke="#AEB4E8" stroke-width="0.75" opacity="0.14"/>
    </pattern>
  </defs>
  <rect width="100%" height="100%" fill="url(#admizz-facets)"/>
</svg>
